[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The operator chooses a different word for a ruled term, and every narrative that used it is flagged

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[USE_CASE]
UID: UC-RENAME-A-TERM
TITLE: The operator chooses a different word for a ruled term, and every narrative that used it is flagged
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The operator decides "joint" should be another word. They retitle the term
narrative and supersede its ruling. The fingerprint check then reports every
narrative that Cites the term as drifted, the view shows each drifted
citation beside the narrative that carries it, and each is re-read and
re-signed or rewritten. Nothing else has to be remembered.
<<<
